# run-bin: the release binary runs under memcheck with --target-processes application-only and must start no CUDA-using child; several lines per binary are allowed (smallest runs)
rcsr-gpu-bench      *  run-bin  --batch 64 --reps 1 --depth 3
rcsr                *  run-bin  calibrate --gpu --no-enrich --out target/sanitizer-calibration.json
rcsr                *  run-bin  --data examples/sine.csv --target y --vars x --generations 8 --pop 24 --seed 5 --metric squared --gpu
reselect               *  no-cuda-app-only  every rcsr child runs with RCSR_GPU=0 (tests/common/rcsr.rs), so no CUDA call in the test process or its children; memcheck with --target-processes application-only does not trace the children
retire                 *  no-cuda-app-only  every rcsr child runs with RCSR_GPU=0 (tests/common/rcsr.rs), so no CUDA call in the test process or its children; memcheck with --target-processes application-only does not trace the children
trials                 *  no-cuda-app-only  every rcsr child runs with RCSR_GPU=0 (tests/common/rcsr.rs), so no CUDA call in the test process or its children; memcheck with --target-processes application-only does not trace the children; its measurement test is ignored
